# Redirects that ALREADY EXIST on fitroofingco.com today.
#
# Nothing here is new. The migration itself needs no redirects: every live URL
# keeps its exact path in this repo, so /about/ is about/index.html,
# /hail-damage-roof-texas/ is hail-damage-roof-texas/index.html, and so on.
#
# These rules exist because the LIVE site answers them right now. If the new
# host does not, each of these URLs goes from working (301 -> a real page) to
# dead (404), and that is the change that would cost backlinks. Every rule was
# checked against live on 15 September 2026 — by tools/discover.mjs for the ones
# linked from the site, and by direct requests for the patterns.
#
# Exact rules are listed with and without their trailing slash: the live site
# answers both forms, and relying on a host to normalise that is how a working
# URL quietly becomes a 404 on cutover.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>, Netlify / Cloudflare Pages style. First match
# wins, so the specific rules sit above the patterns. `:name` matches one path
# segment and `*` matches the rest. tools/serve.mjs replays this file locally.

